    "Id": "vehiclechassisdef_gerrida_GDR-Prime",
    "Name": "Gerrida",
    "Details": "The Prime configuration of the Gerrida, the Society's super-heavy hovertank whose flotation hull lets it keep fighting on water, was derived from the first prototype. Twelve LRM-5 launchers and a Large Pulse Laser fill its turret, and a large ammunition supply that includes Swarm missiles gives it superb endurance and more tactical options. An Active Probe and a Remote Sensor Dispenser improve its awareness of the battlefield for greater coordination.\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Biome Restrictions: None.</color></b>\n\n<b><color=#ffcc00>Movement: 7/11 hexes / 210/330 meters.</color></b>\n\n<color=#ffcc00><b>Armor:</b> Ferro-Lamellor (C)\n<b>Structure:</b> Structure\n<b>Values       A        S  </b>\n<b>Front</b>       225     70\n<b>Left</b>         180     70\n<b>Right</b>       180     70\n<b>Rear</b>        150     70\n<b>Turret</b>      200     70\n\n<b>Total</b>      935    350</color>\n\n<color=#ff0000>Quirk: Distracting</color>\n\n<color=#ffcc00> Omni Vehicle</color>",
    "Icon": "Gerrida"
  },
  "YangsThoughts": "Twelve LRM launchers? That’s one hell of a way to make it rain. The Large Pulse Laser gives the Gerrida something accurate to fall back on, while the Active Probe and Remote Sensors help it find targets for all those missiles. Just keep an eye on the ammo bins—this thing can empty them faster than you’d think.",
